{"context":"Anvil v2 changes vocabulary (adapter → standard), distribution (closed-set discovery → registry), and repository topology (Core + independent standard repositories) while preserving the lifecycle mechanisms v1.x already proves (§1.2: this is an evolution, not a rewrite). Existing users, installed v1.x adapters, and CI workflows must survive the transition. ADR-024 governs contract version compatibility policy; this ADR governs the migration and compatibility framework that carries v1.x users into v2. Source: ADR-028-migration-and-compatibility-framework.md Date:2026-08-03 Status:Proposed.","decision":"- **Adapter → standard mapping.** The v2 migration guide carries a mapping table from v1.x adapters to delivery lifecycle standards. Installed v1.x adapters are recognized, migrated, and validated against the declared contract version (§12.3). Compatibility is declared, validated, and recorded — not assumed (A2).\n- **Dual-run window.** Old and new vocabulary coexist; the registry and closed-set discovery coexist until the switch-over gate (§12.4). Within the window, either path resolves lifecycle content.\n- **Ordered extraction.** Framework packages → template content → config knowledge → adapter binaries (§6.5). Each extraction preserves the subprocess contract; the engine keeps working against extracted standards from the first extraction (contract-stable migration).\n- **v1.x command sur","consequences":"**Positive:** existing users keep working through the transition; CI continuity; each extraction step is verifiable; the migration path is documented and exercised (Phase 6 gate).\n\n**Negative:** dual vocabulary and dual discovery add surface during the window; warnings add output noise; the migration guide must be maintained as a living document; config key renames (e.g., `project.adapter` → `project.standard`) are a separate governed decision (ADR-032).","alternativesConsidered":"Considered\n\n- **Hard cut-over.** Rejected: breaks existing users and CI overnight, contradicting the not-a-rewrite stance (§1.2) and success criterion 6 (\"the v1.x lifecycle remains functional throughout the transition\").\n- **Indefinite dual-run.** Rejected: unbounded maintenance of two vocabularies and two discovery paths; the CLI deprecation window is event-bounded (switch-over gate, §12.4) and the contract-major window is bounded by ADR-024.\n- **v1.x adapters remain in Core as permanent conte"}